# qwen3:8b pinned to fit a 6 GB card.
#
# Ollama's own fit estimator leaves ~2 GB of a 6141 MiB RTX 4050 unused and
# parks 25% of the layers on the CPU. The GPU then idles at 0-14% waiting on
# them and throughput collapses to CPU speed: 15.6 tok/s measured, against
# 34.6 tok/s with every layer resident. Over a 7,769-pair pass that is the
# difference between an overnight run and a fortnight.
#
# num_gpu 99 means "all of them" - it is a ceiling, not a count.
# num_ctx 4096 is sized for the longest prompt (~2,000 tokens) plus bakeoff's
# 1,600-token output ceiling, with headroom. A smaller window truncates a
# reasoning model mid-JSON, which the scorer then reads as UNPARSEABLE.
#
# Requires OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1 and OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 on the
# server, which is what shrinks the KV cache enough for this to fit.
#
#   ollama create qwen3-8b-gpu -f backend/Modelfile.qwen3-8b-gpu
#   ollama ps        # must read 100% GPU

FROM qwen3:8b

PARAMETER num_gpu 99
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
PARAMETER temperature 0.0
